# Project Architecture
- Framework: React Native with Expo (App Router `app/` directory).
- Workflow: Dual-machine setup. Code is written on Windows. Native builds and testing occur on macOS.

# 🚨 CRITICAL GUARDRAILS 🚨
1. NEVER modify `android/build.gradle`, `android/app/build.gradle`, or `ios/Podfile`. Custom patches are applied on the Mac to handle missing binaries. Overwriting these will destroy the native builds.
2. DO NOT use `ffmpeg-kit-react-native`. The package is dead and its binaries are deleted from Maven/CocoaPods.
3. YOU MUST USE `@sheehanmunim/react-native-ffmpeg` for all FFmpeg imports and logic.

# Agent Workflow
1. Write code, build UI, and handle logic on Windows.
2. When a feature is complete, use Git to commit and push to `main` so the macOS machine can pull and compile the native apps.